  "alternatives": [],
  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Medicaid Kerendia Criteria Version 2; Original: 9/23/2021; Effective: 01/1/2024; Updated: 11/21/2025.",
    "Closed CKD associated with T2DM and heart failure with LVEF ≥40% pathways use indication when gates. Baseline lab submission and thresholds, specialty/consultation, and therapy alternatives use attestations; supporting documentation requires manual review.",
    "Cautions (notes only): decreased kidney function and higher baseline potassium increase risk; monitor serum potassium and adjust dose as needed. Avoid grapefruit or grapefruit juice. May cause hyperkalemia, hypotension, and hyponatremia.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 6 months with disease improvement and/or stabilization OR improvement in slope of decline (based on UACR or eGFR), and no developed hyperkalemia. Manual review required.",
    "Quantity (notes only): 30 tablets per 30 days (10mg and 20mg strengths). Quantity enforcement requires manual review."
  ],
